IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part VIII.5 (Temporary Measures to Facilitate Access to Benefits):
-- Waiting Period (s 153.191), Rate of Benefits (s 153.192), Medical Certificate (s 153.1921), Deductions from Benefits
-- (s 153.193), Disqualification and Disentitlement (s 153.194) and Claim Procedure (s 153.195).
-- Written by piece ei6 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is
-- claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Seat: a person who has lost work and asks whether they must wait, how much they would receive, what they must
-- provide and what may be deducted.
--
-- CESSATION. As in ei6-part-8-5-access, a rule limited by s 153.196 takes the BOOLEAN "Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply
-- under section 153.196". A rule that changes a figure or a period returns a MAYBE: NOTHING means the section does not
-- apply to this claimant (so s 14, reg 35 and so on, outside this piece, decide).

§ `Section 153.191 - waiting period`

-- (1): despite sections 13 and 152.15, a claimant need not serve a waiting period if the claim is for benefits under
-- Part I, VII.1 or VIII and the benefit period begins on or before October 25, 2020.
-- src:3014 | 153.191 (1) Despite sections 13 and 152.15, a claimant need not serve a waiting period if the claim is in respect of benefits under Part I, VII.1 or VIII and the benefit period begins on or before October 25, 2020.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.191(1) (src:3014)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 153.191(1) the last day on which a benefit period may begin for the waiting period to be waived` MEANS YearMonthDay 2020 10 25

-- src:3014 | 153.191 (1) Despite sections 13 and 152.15, a claimant need not serve a waiting period if the claim is in respect of benefits under Part I, VII.1 or VIII and the benefit period begins on or before October 25, 2020.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.191(1) (src:3014)
GIVEN `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Part under which the benefits are claimed` IS A `Part of the Act`
      `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.191(1) the claimant need not serve a waiting period` IF
        `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
    AND (   `the Part under which the benefits are claimed` EQUALS `Part I`
         OR `the Part under which the benefits are claimed` EQUALS `Part VII.1`
         OR `the Part under which the benefits are claimed` EQUALS `Part VIII`)
    AND `the first day of the benefit period` AT MOST `s 153.191(1) the last day on which a benefit period may begin for the waiting period to be waived`

-- (1.1): a claimant who receives benefits under section 21 or 152.03 need not serve a waiting period.
-- src:3016 | (1.1) Despite sections 13 and 152.15, a claimant who receives benefits under section 21 or 152.03 need not serve a waiting period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.191(1.1) (src:3016)
GIVEN `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `receives benefits under section 21 or 152.03` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.191(1.1) the claimant need not serve a waiting period` IF
        `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
    AND `receives benefits under section 21 or 152.03`

-- (2): the claimant may nonetheless serve the waiting period if entitled to receive a payment referred to in
-- subsection 37(1) or 38(1) of the Regulations during it. Read as applying to the claimant of (1) and of (1.1) alike
-- (fork F-ei6-12 in NOTES.md).
-- src:3018 | (2) The claimant may nonetheless serve the waiting period if they are entitled to receive a payment referred to in subsection 37(1) or 38(1) of the Employment Insurance Regulations during that period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.191(2) (src:3018)
GIVEN `the claimant need not serve a waiting period under subsection (1) or (1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is entitled to receive a payment referred to in subsection 37(1) or 38(1) of the Employment Insurance Regulations during that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.191(2) the claimant may nonetheless serve the waiting period` IF
        `the claimant need not serve a waiting period under subsection (1) or (1.1)`
    AND `is entitled to receive a payment referred to in subsection 37(1) or 38(1) of the Employment Insurance Regulations during that period`

-- (3): subsections 40(6) and 40.1(2) of the Regulations do not apply to a waiting period to which (1) applies.
-- src:3020 | (3) Subsections 40(6) and 40.1(2) of the Employment Insurance Regulations do not apply to any waiting period to which subsection (1) applies.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.191(3) (src:3020)
GIVEN `the waiting period is one to which subsection (1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.191(3) subsections 40(6) and 40.1(2) of the Regulations apply to the waiting period` IF
    NOT (`the waiting period is one to which subsection (1) applies`)

§ `Section 153.192 - weekly insurable earnings`

-- The floor of $909 and the day from which it applies, carried as values (dates are data).
-- src:3024 | 153.192 (1) Despite subsection 14(2), the weekly insurable earnings of a claimant whose benefit period begins on or after September 27, 2020 are deemed to be the greater of
-- src:3025 | (a) the claimant’s insurable earnings in the calculation period referred to in subsection 14(4), divided by the number of weeks in that period in which they had insurable earnings, and
-- src:3026 | (b) $909.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.192(1) (src:3024-3026)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 153.192 the floor of the weekly insurable earnings` MEANS 909

-- src:3024 | 153.192 (1) Despite subsection 14(2), the weekly insurable earnings of a claimant whose benefit period begins on or after September 27, 2020 are deemed to be the greater of
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.192(1) (src:3024)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 153.192 the first day on which a benefit period begins for the floor to apply` MEANS YearMonthDay 2020 9 27

-- (1): despite subsection 14(2), the weekly insurable earnings of a claimant whose benefit period begins on or after
-- September 27, 2020 are deemed to be the greater of (a) the insurable earnings in the calculation period of 14(4)
-- divided by the number of weeks in that period in which they had insurable earnings, and (b) $909. With no week of
-- insurable earnings, (a) cannot be worked out, and the text does not say what then: NOTHING (fork F-ei6-13).
-- src:3024 | 153.192 (1) Despite subsection 14(2), the weekly insurable earnings of a claimant whose benefit period begins on or after September 27, 2020 are deemed to be the greater of
-- src:3025 | (a) the claimant’s insurable earnings in the calculation period referred to in subsection 14(4), divided by the number of weeks in that period in which they had insurable earnings, and
-- src:3026 | (b) $909.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.192(1) (src:3024-3026)
GIVEN `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the insurable earnings in the calculation period referred to in subsection 14(4)` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 14(4) (piece ei1)
      `the number of weeks in that period in which the claimant had insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 14(4) (piece ei1)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.192(1) the weekly insurable earnings of the claimant are deemed to be` IS
    IF     `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
       AND `the first day of the benefit period` AT LEAST `s 153.192 the first day on which a benefit period begins for the floor to apply`
       AND `the number of weeks in that period in which the claimant had insurable earnings` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (IF `the insurable earnings in the calculation period referred to in subsection 14(4)` DIVIDED BY `the number of weeks in that period in which the claimant had insurable earnings` GREATER THAN `s 153.192 the floor of the weekly insurable earnings`
               THEN `the insurable earnings in the calculation period referred to in subsection 14(4)` DIVIDED BY `the number of weeks in that period in which the claimant had insurable earnings`
               ELSE `s 153.192 the floor of the weekly insurable earnings`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): for a self-employed person whose benefit period begins on or after that day, a result of dividing the aggregate
-- of the amounts in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b) by 52 that is less than $909 is deemed to be $909.
-- src:3028 | (2) Despite subsection 152.16(1), if a self-employed person’s benefit period begins on or after September 27, 2020 and the result obtained by dividing the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b) by 52 is less than $909, the result is deemed to be $909.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.192(2) (src:3028)
GIVEN `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 152.16 (piece ei5)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.192(2) the result of dividing the aggregate by 52, for a self-employed person` IS
    IF     `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
       AND `the first day of the benefit period` AT LEAST `s 153.192 the first day on which a benefit period begins for the floor to apply`
    THEN JUST (IF `the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)` DIVIDED BY 52 LESS THAN `s 153.192 the floor of the weekly insurable earnings`
               THEN `s 153.192 the floor of the weekly insurable earnings`
               ELSE `the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)` DIVIDED BY 52)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3): for a fisher, despite paragraph 8.1(a) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations (not among the
-- inputs), the greater of the amount determined under that paragraph and $909.
-- src:3030 | (3) Despite paragraph 8.1(a) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations, the weekly insurable earnings of a fisher whose benefit period begins on or after September 27, 2020 are deemed to be the greater of the amount determined under that paragraph and $909.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.192(3) (src:3030)
GIVEN `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the weekly insurable earnings determined under paragraph 8.1(a) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.192(3) the weekly insurable earnings of the fisher are deemed to be` IS
    IF     `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
       AND `the first day of the benefit period` AT LEAST `s 153.192 the first day on which a benefit period begins for the floor to apply`
    THEN JUST (IF `the weekly insurable earnings determined under paragraph 8.1(a) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations` GREATER THAN `s 153.192 the floor of the weekly insurable earnings`
               THEN `the weekly insurable earnings determined under paragraph 8.1(a) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations`
               ELSE `s 153.192 the floor of the weekly insurable earnings`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 153.1921 - medical certificate`

-- (1): for subsection 40(1) of the Regulations, the requirement to provide a medical certificate completed by a medical
-- doctor or other medical professional is suspended, unless otherwise indicated by the Commission.
-- src:3034 | 153.1921 (1) For the purpose of applying subsection 40(1) of the Employment Insurance Regulations, the requirement for a claimant to provide a medical certificate to the Commission completed by a medical doctor or other medical professional is suspended, unless otherwise indicated by the Commission.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1921(1) (src:3034)
GIVEN `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has indicated otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1921(1) the requirement to provide a medical certificate under subsection 40(1) of the Regulations is suspended` IF
        `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
    AND NOT (`the Commission has indicated otherwise`)

-- (2): for sections 23.1, 23.2, 23.3 and 152.06 to 152.062, the Commission may suspend the requirement.
-- src:3036 | (2) For the purpose of applying any of sections 23.1, 23.2, 23.3 and 152.06 to 152.062, the Commission may suspend the requirement for a claimant to provide a medical certificate completed by a medical doctor or other medical professional.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1921(2) (src:3036)
GIVEN `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is for benefits under one of sections 23.1, 23.2, 23.3 and 152.06 to 152.062` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has suspended the requirement for the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1921(2) the requirement to provide a medical certificate is suspended for the claimant` IF
        `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
    AND `the claim is for benefits under one of sections 23.1, 23.2, 23.3 and 152.06 to 152.062`
    AND `the Commission has suspended the requirement for the claimant`

-- src:3036 | (2) For the purpose of applying any of sections 23.1, 23.2, 23.3 and 152.06 to 152.062, the Commission may suspend the requirement for a claimant to provide a medical certificate completed by a medical doctor or other medical professional.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1921(2) (src:3036)
GIVEN `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is for benefits under one of sections 23.1, 23.2, 23.3 and 152.06 to 152.062` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1921(2) the Commission may suspend the requirement to provide a medical certificate` IF
        `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
    AND `the claim is for benefits under one of sections 23.1, 23.2, 23.3 and 152.06 to 152.062`

§ `Section 153.193 - exclusions from earnings`

-- (a): pay or earnings referred to in subsection 36(8), (9) or (19) of the Regulations are excluded from the earnings
-- of section 35 of the Regulations if (i) the benefit period begins on or after September 27, 2020, or (ii) the pay or
-- earnings are declared on or after that day and would otherwise have been allocated under section 36 to a week
-- beginning on or after it.
-- src:3060 | 153.193 The following are to be excluded from the earnings referred to in section 35 of the Employment Insurance Regulations:
-- src:3061 | (a) any pay or earnings referred to in subsection 36(8), (9) or (19) of those Regulations if
-- src:3062 | (i) the claimant’s benefit period begins on or after September 27, 2020, or
-- src:3063 | (ii) the pay or earnings are declared to the Commission on or after September 27, 2020 and would otherwise have been allocated under section 36 of those Regulations to a week beginning on or after September 27, 2020; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.193(a) (src:3060-3063)
GIVEN `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is pay or earnings referred to in subsection 36(8), (9) or (19) of the Employment Insurance Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the pay or earnings are declared to the Commission` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the week to which they would otherwise have been allocated under section 36 of the Regulations` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.193(a) the pay or earnings are excluded from the earnings referred to in section 35 of the Regulations` IF
        `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
    AND `is pay or earnings referred to in subsection 36(8), (9) or (19) of the Employment Insurance Regulations`
    AND (   `the first day of the benefit period` AT LEAST (YearMonthDay 2020 9 27)
         OR (    `the day on which the pay or earnings are declared to the Commission` AT LEAST (YearMonthDay 2020 9 27)
             AND `the first day of the week to which they would otherwise have been allocated under section 36 of the Regulations` AT LEAST (YearMonthDay 2020 9 27)))

-- (b): of payments paid to a claimant as an insured person for the first week for which benefits are payable, if the
-- waiting period has been waived under subsection 153.191(1), (i) the portion of a payment referred to in subsection
-- 37(1) of the Regulations that does not exceed 95% of normal weekly earnings from the employment, and (ii) despite
-- paragraph 38(1)(a) of the Regulations, the portion of a payment referred to in subsection 38(1) that does not exceed
-- normal weekly earnings from the employment.
-- src:3064 | (b) any of the following portions of payments that are paid to a claimant as an insured person for the first week for which benefits are payable, if their waiting period has been waived under subsection 153.191(1):
-- src:3065 | (i) the portion of any payments referred to in subsection 37(1) of those Regulations that does not exceed 95% of the claimant’s normal weekly earnings from the employment to which the payments relate, and
-- src:3066 | (ii) despite paragraph 38(1)(a) of those Regulations, the portion of any payments referred to in subsection 38(1) of those Regulations that does not exceed the claimant’s normal weekly earnings from the employment to which the payments relate.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.193(b) (src:3064-3066)
DECLARE `ei6 Kind of payment in section 153.193(b)` IS ONE OF
    `ei6 a payment referred to in subsection 37(1) of the Regulations`
    `ei6 a payment referred to in subsection 38(1) of the Regulations`

-- src:3064 | (b) any of the following portions of payments that are paid to a claimant as an insured person for the first week for which benefits are payable, if their waiting period has been waived under subsection 153.191(1):
-- src:3065 | (i) the portion of any payments referred to in subsection 37(1) of those Regulations that does not exceed 95% of the claimant’s normal weekly earnings from the employment to which the payments relate, and
-- src:3066 | (ii) despite paragraph 38(1)(a) of those Regulations, the portion of any payments referred to in subsection 38(1) of those Regulations that does not exceed the claimant’s normal weekly earnings from the employment to which the payments relate.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.193(b) (src:3064-3066)
GIVEN `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the waiting period has been waived under subsection 153.191(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is paid to the claimant as an insured person for the first week for which benefits are payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `ei6 Kind of payment in section 153.193(b)`
      `the amount of the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from the employment to which the payment relates` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.193(b) the portion of the payment that is excluded from the earnings referred to in section 35 of the Regulations` IS
    IF     `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
       AND `the waiting period has been waived under subsection 153.191(1)`
       AND `the payment is paid to the claimant as an insured person for the first week for which benefits are payable`
    THEN CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `ei6 a payment referred to in subsection 37(1) of the Regulations` THEN
             JUST (IF `the amount of the payment` GREATER THAN 95% TIMES `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from the employment to which the payment relates`
                   THEN 95% TIMES `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from the employment to which the payment relates`
                   ELSE `the amount of the payment`)
         WHEN `ei6 a payment referred to in subsection 38(1) of the Regulations` THEN
             JUST (IF `the amount of the payment` GREATER THAN `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from the employment to which the payment relates`
                   THEN `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from the employment to which the payment relates`
                   ELSE `the amount of the payment`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 153.194 - employment for the purposes of sections 30 to 33`

-- Despite paragraph 29(a), for the purposes of sections 30 to 33 employment refers to any employment of the claimant
-- (a) within their qualifying period, but no earlier than 12 weeks before the Sunday referred to in paragraph 10(1)(a),
-- or (b) within their benefit period. An employment is "within" a period when any part of it falls in the period
-- (assumed, not ruled: fork F-ei6-11 in NOTES.md). Twelve weeks is 84 days.
-- src:3070 | 153.194 Despite paragraph 29(a), for the purposes of sections 30 to 33, employment refers to any employment of the claimant
-- src:3071 | (a) within their qualifying period, but no earlier than 12 weeks before the Sunday referred to in paragraph 10(1)(a); or
-- src:3072 | (b) within their benefit period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.194 (src:3070-3072)
GIVEN `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of the employment` IS A `Period of days`
      `the qualifying period` IS A `Period of days`  -- out of range: section 8 (piece ei1)
      `the benefit period` IS A `Period of days`  -- out of range: sections 9 and 10 (piece ei1)
      `the Sunday referred to in paragraph 10(1)(a)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.194 the employment is employment for the purposes of sections 30 to 33` IF
        `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
    AND (   (    `the period of the employment`'s `first day of the period` AT MOST `the qualifying period`'s `last day of the period`
             AND `the period of the employment`'s `last day of the period` AT LEAST (IF `the qualifying period`'s `first day of the period` AT LEAST `the Sunday referred to in paragraph 10(1)(a)` MINUS `weeks as days` 12
                                                                                       THEN `the qualifying period`'s `first day of the period`
                                                                                       ELSE `the Sunday referred to in paragraph 10(1)(a)` MINUS `weeks as days` 12))
         OR (    `the period of the employment`'s `first day of the period` AT MOST `the benefit period`'s `last day of the period`
             AND `the period of the employment`'s `last day of the period` AT LEAST `the benefit period`'s `first day of the period`))

§ `Section 153.195 - information`

-- Despite paragraph 51(a), the Commission may, but is not required to, give the claimant and the employer the
-- opportunity referred to in that paragraph: the claimant has no claim to it while this section applies.
-- src:3076 | 153.195 Despite paragraph 51(a), the Commission may, but is not required to, give the claimant and the employer the opportunity referred to in that paragraph.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.195 (src:3076)
GIVEN `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.195 the Commission is not required to give the claimant and the employer the opportunity referred to in paragraph 51(a)` IF
    `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
